5. ETHICAL RESTRICTIONS

The permissions granted in Sections 1 to 3 are expressly contingent upon your continuous
compliance with the following ethical standards. AGIT shall not be used by any person or
entity for any systems, activities, or other uses that violate any Human Rights Laws.

"Human Rights Laws" means any applicable laws, regulations, or rules (collectively, "Laws")
that protect human, civil, labor, privacy, political, environmental, security, economic, due
process, or similar rights; provided, however, that such Laws are consistent and not in
conflict with Human Rights Principles.

Where the Human Rights Laws of more than one jurisdiction are applicable or in conflict with
respect to the use of AGIT, the Human Rights Laws that are most protective of the individuals
or groups harmed shall apply. In particular you SHALL NOT, directly or indirectly:

- infringe upon any person's right to life or security of person, engage in extrajudicial
  killings, or commit violence (UN Universal Declaration of Human Rights, Art. 3);
- hold any person in slavery, servitude, or forced labor (UN UDHR, Art. 4);
- torture or subject any person to cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment or punishment
  (UN UDHR, Art. 5);
- discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, sexual orientation, race, ethnicity, nationality,
  religion, caste, age, or disability (UN UDHR, Art. 7);
- arbitrarily interfere with any person's privacy, family, home or correspondence
  (UN UDHR, Art. 12);
- participate in mass surveillance programs, conduct military combat operations, or supply
  products/services directly to law enforcement agencies engaging in human rights abuses;
- engage in mineral or fossil fuel exploration, extraction, or sales listed on the Carbon
  Underground 200 index;
- commit ecocide or acts causing severe, widespread, or long-term damage to the natural
  environment;
- interfere with workers' rights to associate and organize collectively
  (ILO Convention No. 87).

Any breach of this section automatically and immediately terminates all rights granted under
